Subject: [PATCH] TJS2: finish native cleanup after shutdown finalizer errors

A finalizer exception previously skipped native instance invalidation and
member release, leaving the VM/cache and timer references alive. Only during
host-owned shutdown, log and suppress a failing or budget-interrupted script
finalizer so native invalidation and member release still execute. Explicit
script invalidation outside shutdown preserves upstream exception behavior.

Tested-by: tests/test_krkr_tjs2_source_admission.py focused git-apply unittest; forced Android CMake configure; Krkr throwing/infinite finalizer and timer recovery instrumentation

--- a/src/core/tjs2/tjsObject.cpp
+++ b/src/core/tjs2/tjsObject.cpp
@@ -20,6 +20,8 @@

 namespace TJS
 {
+extern bool TJSHostIsShuttingDown();
+extern void TJSHostReportFinalizerFailure();

 //---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 // utility functions
@@ -455,8 +457,16 @@
 	// call this object's "finalize"
 	if(CallFinalize)
 	{
-		FuncCall(0, finalize_name.c_str(), finalize_name.GetHint(), NULL, 0,
-			NULL, this);
+		try
+		{
+			FuncCall(0, finalize_name.c_str(), finalize_name.GetHint(), NULL, 0,
+				NULL, this);
+		}
+		catch(...)
+		{
+			if(!TJSHostIsShuttingDown()) throw;
+			TJSHostReportFinalizerFailure();
+		}
 	}

 	for(tjs_int i=TJS_MAX_NATIVE_CLASS-1; i>=0; i--)
